WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.029
The accepted schedule specifies valve
model

2
00:00:03.149 --> 00:00:06.115
A, while the installed plate shows model
B.

3
00:00:06.235 --> 00:00:09.200
Record the mismatch and its exact
location.

4
00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.148
Do not decide from the model number alone

5
00:00:12.268 --> 00:00:14.682
whether the difference is harmless.

6
00:00:14.802 --> 00:00:18.043
Assess relevant materials, connection,
cleaning

7
00:00:18.163 --> 00:00:22.094
and functional implications with the
responsible experts.

8
00:00:22.214 --> 00:00:24.753
Retain the original observation even

9
00:00:24.873 --> 00:00:27.701
if the supplier later replaces the valve.

10
00:00:28.321 --> 00:00:31.286
Correction may restore the specified
valve,

11
00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:35.889
or a proposed design change may require an
authorized assessment.

12
00:00:36.009 --> 00:00:38.009
These are not the same route.

13
00:00:38.129 --> 00:00:42.819
Do not revise the acceptance criterion
merely to match what arrived.

14
00:00:42.939 --> 00:00:46.525
Define what verification follows the
approved action

15
00:00:46.645 --> 00:00:50.438
and whether earlier checks or later tests
are affected.

16
00:00:50.558 --> 00:00:55.041
Keep the decision and supporting rationale
linked to the finding.

17
00:00:55.661 --> 00:00:59.868
A purchase order for the replacement is
not closure evidence.

18
00:00:59.988 --> 00:01:01.988
After the authorized action,

19
00:01:02.108 --> 00:01:05.004
obtain the specified installation evidence

20
00:01:05.124 --> 00:01:07.607
and assess any related implications.

21
00:01:07.727 --> 00:01:09.727
Retain the original failure

22
00:01:09.847 --> 00:01:13.019
and the subsequent result as separate
records.

23
00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:16.588
A clean second result should not erase the
history

24
00:01:16.708 --> 00:01:20.708
or imply that the first configuration had
always complied.

25
00:01:21.328 --> 00:01:23.461
Annex 15 permits conditional

26
00:01:23.581 --> 00:01:28.685
approval to proceed to the next
qualification stage following a documented

27
00:01:28.805 --> 00:01:33.494
assessment that there is no significant
impact on the next activity.

28
00:01:33.614 --> 00:01:36.511
Responsible authorization is still needed.

29
00:01:36.631 --> 00:01:39.426
For example, an unresolved gasket issue

30
00:01:39.546 --> 00:01:42.373
may prevent wetted-system challenges even

31
00:01:42.493 --> 00:01:46.976
if a separately assessed dry control-
display check could proceed.

32
00:01:47.096 --> 00:01:49.855
This activity-specific dry-check example

33
00:01:49.975 --> 00:01:52.664
is a practical teaching recommendation,

34
00:01:52.784 --> 00:01:56.991
not wording prescribed by the Annex or
permission to proceed.

35
00:01:57.111 --> 00:02:02.285
Do not use a high completion percentage as
a substitute for the assessment.
